<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<!-- Deploy wwwroot contents to the app's root, not _content/SpawnDev.WebTorrent/ -->
		<!-- Required for service worker scope — SW must be at app root to intercept all requests -->
		<StaticWebAssetBasePath Condition="$(StaticWebAssetBasePath) == ''">/</StaticWebAssetBasePath>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
		<Version>3.1.3-rc.11</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>v3.1.3-rc.11: Two-popup handshake-destroy race — paired fix for `ComputeSwarm_Benchmark_RoundTrips_BetweenTwoPopups`. (a) RtcPeer.OnDataChannel: when the channel arrives already in readyState="open" (responder edge case with SipSorcery or browser OnDataChannel), defer EmitConnect one tick via Task.Run instead of firing synchronously. Synchronous firing runs before the Torrent layer subscribes simplePeer.OnConnect, so the connect event goes nowhere and the peer never handshakes — alternative root cause for peerCount=0 on both popups. (b) Torrent.AddPeer OnHandshake: deterministic lexicographic PeerId tiebreaker in the duplicate-detection branch. When two clients form multiple concurrent WebRTC connections, both sides complete BT handshakes on N wires and previously both sides independently destroyed the newcomer — coord kept wire-A, worker kept wire-B, each side's remote close killed the other's survivor, peerCount→0. rc.11 makes both sides agree: smaller-PeerId side destroys the newcomer (prior behavior), larger-PeerId side destroys the existing wire instead. Both converge on the same physical connection surviving. Plus gated verbose diagnostic logging in Peer.cs / RtcPeer.cs destroy paths so next regression is visible. No wire-protocol change. v3.1.3-rc.4: RtcPeer.PeerConnection public getter. v3.1.3-rc.3: SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.3-rc.2 (SCTP burst tunables). v3.1.3-rc.2: Pure-v2 multi-file past file 0, single-_push Wire frames, hardened DisposeAsync. v3.1.3-rc.1: SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.3-rc.1 (SctpDataSender reset-race fix).</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
		<DebugType>Embedded</DebugType>
		<NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
		<Title>SpawnDev.WebTorrent</Title>
		<Authors>LostBeard</Authors>
		<Description>Pure C# BitTorrent/WebTorrent client. 15 BEPs, real WebRTC P2P (browser + desktop), DHT with mutable items (BEP 46 — AI agent communication), web seeds, media streaming with seeking via service worker, OPFS storage. Includes webtorrent-sw.js for COI headers + torrent streaming. No JavaScript dependencies. Runs on desktop (.NET + SIPSorcery) and browser (Blazor WASM + SpawnDev.BlazorJS). 444 unit tests.</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>BitTorrent;WebTorrent;P2P;Torrent;Blazor;WebAssembly;WebRTC;DHT;Streaming;MachineLearning;ModelDelivery;SIPSorcery</PackageTags>
		<NoPackageAnalysis>true</NoPackageAnalysis>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Demo.Shared" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="Assets\icon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS" Version="3.5.3" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.AsyncFileSystem" Version="1.2.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS.Cryptography" Version="3.2.0" />
		<!-- SpawnDev.RTC replaces direct SipSorcery dependency - provides cross-platform WebRTC
		     with proven browser-interop SipSorcery fork (SRTP profile fix) bundled inside.
		     PackageReference (not ProjectReference) so CI / GitHub Pages builds work from a
		     standalone SpawnDev.WebTorrent checkout - they don't have the sibling RTC repo.
		     1.1.1 is the minimum version: 1.1.0 declared a dep on public SIPSorcery 10.0.4-pre
		     which doesn't exist on nuget.org; 1.1.1 bundles the fork DLLs inline (ILGPU pattern). -->
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.RTC" Version="1.1.3-rc.3" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="windows" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="linux" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="macos" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
